issues.description:
On GFX1013 (AMD BC-250) the compute queues do not work. PASID TLB invalidation
routed through KIQ corrupts sustained KFD compute workloads.

Two changes fix it, both scoped to GFX1013 so no other part changes behaviour.

The first routes PASID TLB flushes through MMIO instead of KIQ, and on the
GFX1013 PASID path for GFXHUB(0) uses flush type 0 rather than 2, takes the
invalidate semaphore, and skips the KIQ register write path. Gated on
IP_VERSION(10, 1, 3), so every other GMC v10 device keeps the existing path.

```diff
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@ -232,18 +232,28 @@
  *
  * Flush the TLB for the requested page table.
  */
-static void gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb(struct amdgpu_device *adev, uint32_t vmid,
-					uint32_t vmhub, uint32_t flush_type)
+static void gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_internal(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
+					     uint32_t vmid, uint32_t vmhub,
+					     uint32_t flush_type,
+					     bool gfx1013_pasid_path)
 {
-	bool use_semaphore = gmc_v10_0_use_invalidate_semaphore(adev, vmhub);
+	bool use_semaphore;
 	struct amdgpu_vmhub *hub = &adev->vmhub[vmhub];
-	u32 inv_req = hub->vmhub_funcs->get_invalidate_req(vmid, flush_type);
+	u32 inv_req;
 	/* Use register 17 for GART */
 	const unsigned int eng = 17;
 	unsigned char hub_ip = 0;
 	u32 sem, req, ack;
 	unsigned int i;
 	u32 tmp;
+
+	if (gfx1013_pasid_path && vmhub == AMDGPU_GFXHUB(0) &&
+	    flush_type == 2)
+		flush_type = 0;
